-- title:
--   Evaluating an indexed suffix query as an exact raw-prefix count
-- statement:
--   Write $S,\Omega,\Delta$ for machine space, word magnitude, and depth limits. Let finite labeled inputs $A,B,C$ have integer value maps $a,b,c$, and let $p,\delta\in\mathbb Z$. Fix a wanted label $w=(x,\ell,q)$ with $x\in A$, $\ell\in\{-1,0,1\}$, and
--   $$M\mid a(x)\bmod p+\ell p+\delta-\operatorname{key}(q),$$
--   where $M$ is the global block modulus. Let $P$ be a valid length-$k$ prefix of $q$, $k\le J$: it chooses $h$ elements from each of the first $k$ output rows. Put $W=512hJ$, $V=512h(J-k)$, and $r=2h(J-k)$.
--
--   Assume exact left/right source transforms and the retained signed suffix table for $P$, query parameters $t\le r+1$, $b\le r$, $r-t\le b$, and the stated ordered memory and scratch bounds. With $Q=\sum_{j=0}^t\binom rj$, require the contract's address bound, $(Q+1)2^{3V}|B||C|$ word bound, and $d+W+10$ depth bound. The routine returns
--   $$\#\{u\in I:\operatorname{wanted}(u)=w,\ \operatorname{word}(u)|_k=P\},$$
--   where $I$ is the raw representation set induced by $A\times B\times C$. It meets the suffix-query time budget and preserves cells below scratch except the query-mask buffer.
--
--   This connects the numerical suffix query to its reporting count.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingSuffixQueryIndexed.lean#L17-L79

